// Patch the bundled dsh packages for Electron-as-node and workspace behavior.
//
// 1. Folder-picker worker: upstream dsh reads the picked path with
//    `koffi.view(ptr, len)`, which wraps raw native memory in an external
//    ArrayBuffer. Under ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE (how this desktop shell runs the
//    bundled dsh), koffi's error path hits `napi_fatal_error` and the worker
//    process dies with `FATAL ERROR: Error::New napi_get_last_error_info`
//    the moment a folder is selected. Plain Node is unaffected.
// 2. Workspace delete: upstream dsh drops the registration only, so the
//    workspace's conversations resurface under the ungrouped bucket. These
//    patches permanently delete every accounted session (session-persistence
//    delete + jsonl backend delete + registry wiring).
// 3. Session delete: upstream dsh has no way to delete a session. These
//    patches add session.delete end to end (API proxy with a session-live
//    guard, fetch carrier, client runtime) and surface a "删除会话" row action.
// 4. Archive management: upstream dsh has no way to restore an archived
//    session, and the sidebar showed an "已归档" bucket. These patches add
//    workspace.unarchiveSession end to end, move the archived-session list
//    into Settings (unarchive + delete actions), and remove the ungrouped
//    bucket from the sidebar entirely.
//
// The script is the postinstall hook, is idempotent, and becomes a no-op once
// upstream ships its own fixes (the original blocks will no longer match).
// When the dsh dependency is upgraded, delete this script and its package.json
// postinstall entry once the fixes land upstream.
// Usage: node scripts/patch-dsh.mjs
